subproblems.statement:
Let n, ℓ ∈ ℕ and Hⁿ := μHE[n] on ℝ^{n+ℓ}. Assume:
- A ⊆ ℝ^{n+ℓ} is Borel with Hⁿ(A) < ∞, and ϑ : ℝ^{n+ℓ} → ℝ is Hⁿ-integrable on A;
- C ⊆ A is Borel, and x ∈ ℝ^{n+ℓ} is a point at which ϑ is continuous relative to C (ContinuousWithinAt ϑ C x);
- P is a linear subspace that is the approximate tangent space of C at x (Simon Def. 3.1.4; Chapter03.HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt n C x P);
- with μ' := (Hⁿ⌞A).withDensity(‖ϑ‖ₑ), (ρⁿ)⁻¹·μ'.real((A ∖ C) ∩ B_ρ(x)) → 0 as ρ ↓ 0, where B_ρ(x) is the closed ball.
Then P is the approximate tangent space of A at x with respect to ϑ (Simon Def. 3.1.7; Chapter03.HasWeightedApproximateTangentSpaceAt n A ϑ x P).
